<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<FaqItem question="Can I make money with AI-generated videos as an affiliate?">
<p>Yes. AI avatar and text-to-video tools let you produce review, tutorial, and comparison videos without filming. The content quality depends on the script, structure, and editing — not the tool. Affiliates who invest time in good scripts and strong CTAs see the same conversion patterns as traditionally filmed video content. The advantage of AI tools is speed and consistency — you can maintain a publishing schedule that would be impossible with manual filming and editing.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Do YouTube and TikTok penalise AI-generated videos?">
<p>No platform currently penalises AI-generated content automatically. YouTube's policies focus on content quality and viewer experience, regardless of how the video was produced. TikTok's algorithm prioritises engagement metrics — watch time, completion rate, shares — not production method. However, low-effort AI content (generic avatar reading a generic script with no editing) performs poorly because viewers disengage, not because of any platform penalty.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="What is the best AI video tool for beginners?">
<p>For affiliates creating product reviews and tutorials without filming, AI avatar tools like HeyGen offer the smoothest learning curve — write a script, pick an avatar, generate. For content repurposing (turning blog posts into videos), text-to-video tools convert existing written content into video format with minimal effort. See our <a href="/reviews/heygen-review/">HeyGen review</a> for a comprehensive breakdown of one of the leading AI avatar tools.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="How long should an affiliate marketing video be?">
<p>Product overviews and reviews: 3–5 minutes. Comparisons: 5–8 minutes. Tutorials: 5–10 minutes. The optimal length is determined by search intent — if the top-ranking videos for your target keyword average 6 minutes, aim for 6–7 minutes. YouTube's algorithm favours videos that keep viewers watching, and length is secondary to retention. A 4-minute video with 70% retention outperforms an 8-minute video with 30% retention.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="Do I need to show my face in affiliate videos?">
<p>No. AI avatar videos let you create professional-looking content without appearing on camera. Many successful affiliate channels use screen recordings, animations, or AI avatars exclusively. The content quality — script, structure, information value — matters far more than whether the creator's face appears. If you are comfortable on camera, it can build personal trust faster. If you are not, AI avatars and screen recordings are effective alternatives.</p>
</FaqItem>

<FaqItem question="How do I get my first 1,000 views on an AI-generated video?">
<p>Optimise the title for search (include the primary keyword naturally). Write a description with relevant keywords and your affiliate link in the first two lines. Create a custom thumbnail with contrasting colours and clear text. Share the video in relevant online communities — Reddit threads, Facebook groups, forum discussions — where the content genuinely helps answer a question. The first 1,000 views come from search and community distribution, not from the algorithm promoting an unknown channel.</p>
</FaqItem>
